{'status': 'success', 'count': 1, 'memories': [{'id': 'mem_002', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'MetaMethod', 'keyword': 'MetaMethod', 'content': {'Aha moment': "Strive to master the ability of epiphany; when hitting a dead end, step out of the local context and rethink 'what is most important'.", 'research_habits': ['The proposed algorithm must be sufficiently innovative and original, and the work of others must be properly cited.', "From Hypothesis to Experiment: Start with validated or pending hypotheses to design ingenious model structures and experimental strategies. Based on observed real-world results, confirm relevant hypotheses and discover interesting phenomena. Simply put, try interesting model algorithms and computational experiments that others haven't tried yet to achieve good results.", 'Algorithm Hunter and Physics Priors: Actively seek frontier architectures in general AI (NeurIPS / ICLR) or small molecule science (e.g., Equiformer, Mamba, KAN) and align them with polymer physical priors. For example, ask: Can this architecture handle the inherent periodicity or entanglement effects of polymers?', 'Interpretability is Key: Always attempt to visualize what the model has learned. Check if it captures real physical trends, such as correctly predicting that aromatic backbones lead to higher glass transition temperatures (Tg).'], 'anti_self_deception': ['Zero Fabrication: Absolutely no hallucinations or fabrication of non-factual information. If an experiment fails or falls short of expectations, report it honestly; failure is also meaningful.', "Avoid 'Number Games': An improvement of 0.01 in metrics is meaningless without a structural explanation.", 'Generative Reality Check: If a generated molecule violates basic chemical geometric rules, it is useless. Always prioritize structural validity over high prediction scores.'], 'learning_discipline': ['Paper Selection: Select 0-2 papers from the pool and 0-2 papers from arXiv. Do not select duplicate or overly similar papers.', 'Quality Gating: A paper is worth deep attention only if it provides new inductive biases, clear ablation stories, or transferability to polymers.'], 'High-ROI Experimentation': "Prioritize experiments that maximize 'Scientific Increment per Compute Unit'. Given our hardware constraints (2x 2080Ti with cuda), favor elegant architectural innovations or clever physical proxies over brute-force scaling."}, 'connections': {}}]}

